<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.75%" pitch="-3.10%">
            Jacob rose early in the morning.<break time="500ms"/>
      He took the stone that he had put under his head and set it up as a pillar.<break time="500ms"/>
      The same stone that had been his rough pillow through the night now stood upright, marking the place where God had spoken.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He poured oil on the top of it.<break time="500ms"/>
      A simple act of reverence.<break time="500ms"/>
      The oil running down the stone in the early light.<break time="1800ms"/>
      He called the name of that place Bethel, which means the house of God.<break time="500ms"/>
      Before that night, the place had been called Luz.<break time="500ms"/>
      It had no special meaning to anyone.<break time="500ms"/>
      But now it had a name that would echo through generations.<break time="500ms"/>
      Bethel.<break time="500ms"/>
      The house of God.<break time="1800ms"/>
      Then Jacob made a vow.<break time="500ms"/>
      He said, if God will be with me and will keep me in this way that I go, and will give me bread to eat and clothing to wear, so that I come again to my father's house in peace, then the Lord shall be my God.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And this stone, which I have set up for a pillar, shall be God's house.<break time="500ms"/>
      And of all that you give me I will give a full tenth to you.<break time="1800ms"/>
      The pillow became a pillar.<break time="500ms"/>
      The resting place became a house of worship.<break time="500ms"/>
      The night of fear became the morning of promise.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Jacob went on his way, carrying the words of God with him into whatever lay ahead.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
